CollaborationSession retains participants, board, activity, sequence and pending binding transfers in the ordinary shared object pool.
joinName:kind: creates a SessionParticipant, registers it and returns its identity.
activeParticipant: rejects identities outside this session and participants who have left.
leave: validates membership and releases the participant workspace through its leave method.
publish:value:expected:by: validates active membership and exact nonnegative integer revision, compares the current revision atomically, creates a publication if absent, and retains the new typed value. A new name requires revision zero.
unpublish:expected:by: requires an existing present publication and matching revision, then clears its value while preserving a revision tombstone.
publication: returns a present publication or signals that the name is absent or removed.
prepareBinding:for: validates membership and retains a transfer containing the publication value and participant workspace. Return the transfer identity without waiting for the workspace.
releaseBinding: releases a finished transfer.
record: appends attributed serialized activity with an increasing sequence; keep the latest 200 entries.
snapshot returns JSON describing participant, publication and activity state through the narrow runtime snapshot primitive.
